-> for any collection .. align pointer and stick a modulo bloom filter in the n bits

   Dont worry when you fix the pointer compare and if they match with original its an empty
   collection so that saves the dependent load. In addition you could save something off
   the filter itself.


-> Inside the data structure place a real bloom filter use sufficient bits typically 
   128 bits is ok but use more if necessary. 

----> whether to use div based bloom or mod based depends upon the collection. If its an 
      array then you probably want to avoid initializing it all so you want to find out
      uninitialized blocks using div based filters (mod ones wont give contiguity)

----> if its not an array based then use mod based

